<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!--
        The empty set, ∅, for the name.

        The ring is two half arcs rather than one nearly-closed arc, so the stroke has no seam
        where its ends meet. Its outer edge lands at 26 from the centre of the 108 canvas, inside
        the central 66 every launcher is guaranteed to show.
    -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M32,54 A22,22 0 1,1 76,54 A22,22 0 1,1 32,54"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="8" />
    <!--
        The slash deliberately overruns the safe zone. A circular mask shows the central 72 of the
        canvas — a circle of radius 36 — so ends placed just beyond that radius are clipped flush
        to it, and the line reads as running from one side of the icon to the other. Kept flat
        rather than round: a round cap on a stroke this thick reads as a knob on the end of the
        line instead of a line that has been cut off by the edge.
    -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M27.5,80.5 L80.5,27.5"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="8" />
</vector>
